  "checkpoints": [
    {"id": "cp0", "at": 1, "title": "Descent is sequential", "body": "Only f(4) is active at first. It pauses while f(3) runs, and so on, so the stack holds unfinished calls; it does not contain copies running at the same time.", "pause": true, "learnerAction": "continue"},
    {"id": "cp1", "at": 9, "title": "Base case stops the descent", "body": "f(0) is reached last, after f(4), f(3), f(2) and f(1). It returns 1 immediately. Without a base case the calls would keep descending instead of stopping.", "pause": true, "learnerAction": "continue"},
    {"id": "cp2", "at": 15, "title": "Unwinding is LIFO", "body": "f(0) returns first, then f(1), f(2), f(3), f(4). Each caller multiplies its own n by the value returned by the call it was waiting on. The newest frame always leaves first.", "pause": true, "learnerAction": "continue"},
    {"id": "cp3", "at": 21, "title": "Final result", "body": "24 = 4 * 3 * 2 * 1. The stack is empty and every return happened in reverse call order. Check the base case: it was reached at the bottom of the descent, not before the recursive calls.", "pause": true, "learnerAction": "continue"}
  ],
  "narration": [
    {"at": 0, "text": "A recursive call pushes one frame and then waits for the next call."},
    {"at": 6, "text": "The stack grows downward until the base case f(0) is reached."},
    {"at": 10, "text": "The base case returns 1 without making another call."},
    {"at": 18, "text": "Returns pop the stack in reverse order and produce 24."}
  ],
