  "fallback": {
    "text": "The recursive call factorial(4) is not finished immediately. It calls factorial(3) and waits; that call calls factorial(2), which calls factorial(1), which calls factorial(0). These unfinished calls form a stack, with the newest call on top. Only the top call is active, so the calls run one after another, not all at once. At n = 0 the base case returns 1 without calling again. Then the stack unwinds: factorial(1) returns 1, factorial(2) returns 2, factorial(3) returns 6, and factorial(4) returns 24. The base case is reached last in the descent and returns first in the unwind, which is LIFO order."
  },
